(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[12] = [{"v":1,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"एवं सततयुक्ता ये भक्तास्त्वां पर्युपासते ।\nयेचाप्यक्षरमव्यक्तं तेषां के योगवित्तमाः ॥","iast":"evaṃ satatayuktā ye bhaktāstvāṃ paryupāsate |\nyecāpyakṣaramavyaktaṃ teṣāṃ ke yogavittamāḥ ||","read":"evam satatayuktaa ye bhaktaastvaam paryupaasate |\nyechaapyaksharamavyaktam teshaam ke yogavittamaah ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: Those devotees who ever harmonised worship Thee, and those also who worship the Indestructible, the Unmanifested, whether of these is the more learned in yoga?","en2":"Those devotees who, ever-steadfast, thus worship Thee, and those also who worship the Imperishable, the Unmanifested,—which of them are better versed in Yoga?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks Krishna a question. Some faithful people always worship Krishna himself, steady in heart. Others worship the unseen one that never perishes. Which of them knows the way better?"},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"मय्यावेश्य मनो ये मां नित्ययुक्ता उपासते ।\nश्रद्धया परयोपेतास्ते मे युक्ततमा मताः ॥","iast":"mayyāveśya mano ye māṃ nityayuktā upāsate |\nśraddhayā parayopetāste me yuktatamā matāḥ ||","read":"mayyaaveshya mano ye maam nityayuktaa upaasate |\nshraddhayaa parayopetaaste me yuktatamaa mataah ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: They who with mind fixed on Me ever harmonised worship Me, with faith supreme endowed, these, in My opinion, are best in yoga.","en2":"Those who, fixing their mind on Me, worship Me, ever-steadfast, and endowed with supreme Shraddhâ, they in My opinion are the best versed in Yoga.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna answers. Those who fix their minds on him, worship him steadily and have the greatest faith are, in his view, the ones who know the way best."},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये त्वक्षरमनिर्देश्यमव्यक्तं पर्युपासते ।\nसर्वत्रगमचिन्त्यं च कूटस्थमचलं ध्रुवम् ॥","iast":"ye tvakṣaramanirdeśyamavyaktaṃ paryupāsate |\nsarvatragamacintyaṃ ca kūṭasthamacalaṃ dhruvam ||","read":"ye tvaksharamanirdeshyamavyaktam paryupaasate |\nsarvatragamachintyam cha kootasthamachalam dhruvam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They who worship the Indestructible, the Ineffable, the unmanifested, Omnipresent, and Unthinkable, the Unchanging, Immutable, Eternal,","en2":"But those also, who worship the Imperishable, the Indefinable, the Unmanifested, the Omnipresent, the Unthinkable, the Unchangeable, the Immovable, the Eternal,—having subdued all the senses, even-minded everywhere, engaged in the welfare of all beings, verily, they reach only Myself.","en2r":"12.3-4","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna speaks of people who worship the one that never perishes. It cannot be described or seen, or even thought about. It is everywhere, never changes, never moves, and lasts forever."},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"संनियम्येन्द्रियग्रामं सर्वत्र समबुद्धयः ।\nते प्राप्नुवन्ति मामेव सर्वभूतहिते रताः ॥","iast":"saṃniyamyendriyagrāmaṃ sarvatra samabuddhayaḥ |\nte prāpnuvanti māmeva sarvabhūtahite ratāḥ ||","read":"samniyamyendriyagraamam sarvatra samabuddhayah |\nte praapnuvanti maameva sarvabhootahite rataah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Restraining and subduing the senses, regarding everything equally, in the welfare of all rejoicing, these also come unto Me.","en2":"But those also, who worship the Imperishable, the Indefinable, the Unmanifested, the Omnipresent, the Unthinkable, the Unchangeable, the Immovable, the Eternal,—having subdued all the senses, even-minded everywhere, engaged in the welfare of all beings, verily, they reach only Myself.","en2r":"12.3-4","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says these people also come to him, when they control their senses, treat everything equally, and give themselves to the good of all beings."},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"क्लेशोऽधिकतरस्तेषामव्यक्तासक्तचेतसाम् ।\nअव्यक्ता हि गतिर्दुःखं देहवद्भिरवाप्यते ॥","iast":"kleśo’dhikatarasteṣāmavyaktāsaktacetasām |\navyaktā hi gatirduḥkhaṃ dehavadbhiravāpyate ||","read":"klesho'dhikatarasteshaamavyaktaasaktachetasaam |\navyaktaa hi gatirduhkham dehavadbhiravaapyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The difficulty of those whose minds are set on the Unmanifested is greater; for the path of the Unmanifested is hard for the embodied to reach.","en2":"Greater is their trouble whose minds are set on the Unmanifested; for the goal of the Unmanifested is very hard for the embodied to reach.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the way is harder for those whose minds are set on the unseen. For anyone living in a body, that goal is very hard to reach."},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये तु सर्वाणि कर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्पराः ।\nअनन्येनैव योगेन मां ध्यायन्त उपासते ॥","iast":"ye tu sarvāṇi karmāṇi mayi saṃnyasya matparāḥ |\nananyenaiva yogena māṃ dhyāyanta upāsate ||","read":"ye tu sarvaani karmaani mayi samnyasya matparaah |\nananyenaiva yogena maam dhyaayanta upaasate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Those verily who, renouncing all actions in Me and intent on Me, worship meditating on Me, with whole-hearted yoga,","en2":"But those who worship Me, resigning all actions in Me, regarding Me as the Supreme Goal, meditating on Me with single-minded Yoga,—to these whose mind is set on Me, verily, I become ere long, O son of Prithâ, the Saviour out of the ocean of the mortal Samsâra.","en2r":"12.6-7","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna speaks of those who give all their actions over to him. They keep him as their goal, and worship him by thinking of him with their whole heart."},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तेषामहं समुद्धर्ता मृत्युसंसारसागरात् ।\nभवामि नचिरात्पार्थ मय्यावेशितचेतसाम् ॥","iast":"teṣāmahaṃ samuddhartā mṛtyusaṃsārasāgarāt |\nbhavāmi nacirātpārtha mayyāveśitacetasām ||","read":"teshaamaham samuddhartaa mrityusamsaarasaagaraat |\nbhavaami nachiraatpaartha mayyaaveshitachetasaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"These I speedily lift up from the ocean of death and existence, O Pârtha, their minds being fixed on Me.","en2":"But those who worship Me, resigning all actions in Me, regarding Me as the Supreme Goal, meditating on Me with single-minded Yoga,—to these whose mind is set on Me, verily, I become ere long, O son of Prithâ, the Saviour out of the ocean of the mortal Samsâra.","en2r":"12.6-7","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he soon lifts these people out of the ocean of life and death, because their minds are fixed on him."},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मय्येव मन आधत्स्व मयि बुद्धिं निवेशय ।\nनिवसिष्यसि मय्येव अत ऊर्ध्वं न संशयः ॥","iast":"mayyeva mana ādhatsva mayi buddhiṃ niveśaya |\nnivasiṣyasi mayyeva ata ūrdhvaṃ na saṃśayaḥ ||","read":"mayyeva mana aadhatsva mayi buddhim niveshaya |\nnivasishyasi mayyeva ata oordhvam na samshayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Place thy mind in me, into Me let thy Reason enter; then without doubt thou shalt abide in Me hereafter.","en2":"Fix thy mind on Me only, place thy intellect in Me: (then) thou shalt no doubt live in Me hereafter.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna to fix his mind on him and give him his understanding too. Then, without doubt, Arjuna will live in Krishna afterwards."},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अथ चित्तं समाधातुं न शक्नोषि मयि स्थिरम् ।\nअभ्यासयोगेन ततो मामिच्छाप्तुं धनञ्जय ॥","iast":"atha cittaṃ samādhātuṃ na śaknoṣi mayi sthiram |\nabhyāsayogena tato māmicchāptuṃ dhanañjaya ||","read":"atha chittam samaadhaatum na shaknoshi mayi sthiram |\nabhyaasayogena tato maamichchhaaptum dhananjaya ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And if thou art not able firmly to fix thy mind on Me, then by the yoga of practice seek to reach Me, O Dhananjaya.","en2":"If thou art unable to fix thy mind steadily on Me, then by Abhyâsa-Yoga do thou seek to reach Me, O Dhananjaya.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that if Arjuna cannot keep his mind steady on him, he should try to reach him through practice."},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अभ्यासेऽप्यसमर्थोऽसि मत्कर्मपरमो भव ।\nमदर्थमपि कर्माणि कुर्वन् सिद्धिमवाप्स्यसि ॥","iast":"abhyāse’pyasamartho’si matkarmaparamo bhava |\nmadarthamapi karmāṇi kurvan siddhimavāpsyasi ||","read":"abhyaase'pyasamartho'si matkarmaparamo bhava |\nmadarthamapi karmaani kurvan siddhimavaapsyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"If also thou art not equal to constant practice, be intent on My service; performing actions for My sake, thou shalt attain perfection.","en2":"If also thou art unable to practise Abhyâsa, be thou intent on doing actions -for My sake. Even by doing actions for My sake, thou shalt attain perfection.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that if Arjuna cannot keep up steady practice, he should do his actions for the sake of Krishna. Even by doing that, he will reach perfection."},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अथैतदप्यशक्तोऽसि कर्तुं मद्योगमाश्रितः ।\nसर्वकर्मफलत्यागं ततः कुरु यतात्मवान् ॥","iast":"athaitadapyaśakto’si kartuṃ madyogamāśritaḥ |\nsarvakarmaphalatyāgaṃ tataḥ kuru yatātmavān ||","read":"athaitadapyashakto'si kartum madyogamaashritah |\nsarvakarmaphalatyaagam tatah kuru yataatmavaan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"If even to do this thou hast not strength, then, taking refuge in union with Me, renounce all fruit of action with the self controlled.","en2":"If thou art unable to do even this, then taking refuge in Me, abandon the fruit of all action, self-controlled.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that if even this is too hard, Arjuna should take shelter in him, control himself, and give up the fruit of all his actions."},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रेयो हि ज्ञानमभ्यासाज्ज्ञानाद्ध्यानं विशिष्यते ।\nध्यानात्कर्मफलत्यागस्त्यागाच्छान्तिरनन्तरम् ॥","iast":"śreyo hi jñānamabhyāsājjñānāddhyānaṃ viśiṣyate |\ndhyānātkarmaphalatyāgastyāgācchāntiranantaram ||","read":"shreyo hi jnaanamabhyaasaajjnaanaaddhyaanam vishishyate |\ndhyaanaatkarmaphalatyaagastyaagaachchhaantiranantaram ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Better indeed is wisdom than constant-practice; than wisdom, meditation is better; than meditation, renunciation of the fruit of action; on renunciation follows peace.","en2":"Better indeed is knowledge than (blind) Abhyâsa; meditation (with knowledge) is more esteemed than (mere) knowledge; than meditation the renunciation of the fruit of action; peace immediately follows renunciation.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says knowledge is better than practice alone. Meditation is better than knowledge. Better than meditation is giving up the fruit of actions, and peace follows giving it up."},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अद्वेष्टा सर्वभूतानां मैत्रः करुण एव च ।\nनिर्ममो निरहङ्कारः समदुःखसुखः क्षमी ॥","iast":"adveṣṭā sarvabhūtānāṃ maitraḥ karuṇa eva ca |\nnirmamo nirahaṅkāraḥ samaduḥkhasukhaḥ kṣamī ||","read":"adveshtaa sarvabhootaanaam maitrah karuna eva cha |\nnirmamo nirahankaarah samaduhkhasukhah kshamee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who beareth no ill-will to any being, friendly and compassionate, without attachment and egoism, balanced in pleasure and pain, and forgiving,","en2":"He who hates no creature, and is friendly and compassionate towards all, who is free from the feelings of 'I and mine,' even-minded in pain and pleasure, forbearing, ever content, steady in meditation, self-controlled, and possessed of firm conviction, with mind and intellect fixed on Me,—he who is thus devoted to Me, is dear to Me.","en2r":"12.13-14","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna describes a person who hates no creature. He is friendly and kind to all, free from thinking only of \"I\" and \"mine\", calm in pain and pleasure, and forgiving."},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सन्तुष्टः सततं योगी यतात्मा दृढनिश्चयः ।\nमय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः ॥","iast":"santuṣṭaḥ satataṃ yogī yatātmā dṛḍhaniścayaḥ |\nmayyarpitamanobuddhiryo madbhaktaḥ sa me priyaḥ ||","read":"santushtah satatam yogee yataatmaa dridhanishchayah |\nmayyarpitamanobuddhiryo madbhaktah sa me priyah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Ever content, harmonious, with the self-controlled, resolute, with mind and Reason dedicated to Me, he, My devotee, is dear to Me.","en2":"He who hates no creature, and is friendly and compassionate towards all, who is free from the feelings of 'I and mine,' even-minded in pain and pleasure, forbearing, ever content, steady in meditation, self-controlled, and possessed of firm conviction, with mind and intellect fixed on Me,—he who is thus devoted to Me, is dear to Me.","en2r":"12.13-14","rv":null,"kid":"Such a person is always content, steady, self-controlled and firm, with mind and understanding given to Krishna. Krishna says this devoted person is dear to him."},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यस्मान्नोद्विजते लोको लोकान्नोद्विजते च यः ।\nहर्षामर्षभयोद्वेगैर्मुक्तो यः स च मे प्रियः ॥","iast":"yasmānnodvijate loko lokānnodvijate ca yaḥ |\nharṣāmarṣabhayodvegairmukto yaḥ sa ca me priyaḥ ||","read":"yasmaannodvijate loko lokaannodvijate cha yah |\nharshaamarshabhayodvegairmukto yah sa cha me priyah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He from whom the world doth not shrink away, who doth not shrink away from the world, freed from the anxieties of joy, anger, and fear, he is dear to me.","en2":"He by whom the world is not agitated and who cannot be agitated by the world, who is freed from joy, envy, fear and anxiety,—he is dear to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a person who does not upset the world, and is not upset by it, is dear to him. Such a person is not carried away by joy, fear or worry."},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्ष उदासीनो गतव्यथः ।\nसर्वारम्भपरित्यागी यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः ॥","iast":"anapekṣaḥ śucirdakṣa udāsīno gatavyathaḥ |\nsarvārambhaparityāgī yo madbhaktaḥ sa me priyaḥ ||","read":"anapekshah shuchirdaksha udaaseeno gatavyathah |\nsarvaarambhaparityaagee yo madbhaktah sa me priyah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who wants nothing, is pure, expert, passionless, untroubled, renouncing every undertaking, he, My devotee, is dear to Me.","en2":"He who is free from dependence, who is pure, prompt, unconcerned, untroubled, renouncing every undertaking,—he who is thus devoted to Me, is dear to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the devoted person who is dear to him depends on nothing and wants nothing. He is pure, quick to act, calm and untroubled, and gives up every new plan."},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यो न हृष्यति न द्वेष्टि न शोचति न काङ्क्षति ।\nशुभाशुभपरित्यागी भक्तिमान्यः स मे प्रियः ॥","iast":"yo na hṛṣyati na dveṣṭi na śocati na kāṅkṣati |\nśubhāśubhaparityāgī bhaktimānyaḥ sa me priyaḥ ||","read":"yo na hrishyati na dveshti na shochati na kaankshati |\nshubhaashubhaparityaagee bhaktimaanyah sa me priyah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who neither loveth nor hateth, nor grieveth, nor desireth, renouncing good and evil, full of devotion, he is dear to Me.","en2":"He who neither rejoices, nor hates, nor grieves, nor desires, renouncing good and evil, full of devotion, he is dear to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a person who is not carried away by gladness or hate, grief or longing, who gives up both good and evil, and is full of devotion, is dear to him."},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"समः शत्रौ च मित्रे च तथा मानापमानयोः ।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु समः सङ्गविवर्जितः ॥","iast":"samaḥ śatrau ca mitre ca tathā mānāpamānayoḥ |\nśītoṣṇasukhaduḥkheṣu samaḥ saṅgavivarjitaḥ ||","read":"samah shatrau cha mitre cha tathaa maanaapamaanayoh |\nsheetoshnasukhaduhkheshu samah sangavivarjitah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Alike to foe and friend, and also in fame and ignominy, alike in cold and heat, pleasures and pains, destitute of attachment,","en2":"He who is the same to friend and foe, and also in honour and dishonour; who is the same in heat and cold, and in pleasure and pain; who is free from attachment; to whom censure and praise are equal; who is silent, content with anything, homeless, steady-minded, full of devotion,—that man is dear to Me.","en2r":"12.18-19","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna describes a person who is the same to friend and enemy, the same in honour and shame, in cold and heat, and in pleasure and pain. He clings to nothing."},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तुल्यनिन्दास्तुतिर्मौनी सन्तुष्टो येनकेनचित् ।\nअनिकेतः स्थिरमतिर्भक्तिमान्मे प्रियो नरः ॥","iast":"tulyanindāstutirmaunī santuṣṭo yenakenacit |\naniketaḥ sthiramatirbhaktimānme priyo naraḥ ||","read":"tulyanindaastutirmaunee santushto yenakenachit |\naniketah sthiramatirbhaktimaanme priyo narah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Taking equally praise and reproach, silent, wholly content with what cometh, homeless, firm in mind, full of devotion, that man is dear to Me.","en2":"He who is the same to friend and foe, and also in honour and dishonour; who is the same in heat and cold, and in pleasure and pain; who is free from attachment; to whom censure and praise are equal; who is silent, content with anything, homeless, steady-minded, full of devotion,—that man is dear to Me.","en2r":"12.18-19","rv":null,"kid":"He takes praise and blame alike. He is quiet, content with whatever comes, homeless, steady in mind and full of devotion. Krishna says such a person is dear to him."},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये तु धर्म्यामृतमिदं यथोक्तं पर्युपासते ।\nश्रद्दधाना मत्परमा भक्तास्तेऽतीव मे प्रियाः ॥","iast":"ye tu dharmyāmṛtamidaṃ yathoktaṃ paryupāsate |\nśraddadhānā matparamā bhaktāste’tīva me priyāḥ ||","read":"ye tu dharmyaamritamidam yathoktam paryupaasate |\nshraddadhaanaa matparamaa bhaktaaste'teeva me priyaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They verily who partake of this life-giving wisdom as taught herein, endued with faith, I their supreme Object, devotees, they are surpassingly dear to Me.","en2":"And they who follow this Immortal Dharma, as described above, endued with Shraddhâ, regarding Me as the Supreme Goal, and devoted,—they are exceedingly dear to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says those who follow the teaching he has just given, with faith, making him their highest goal and devoted to him, are especially dear to him."}];
